        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fdd3d3de-f667-546f-a26e-07d1eafd0e25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Ashman, Alan Menken\n- Works: “Be Our Guest,” Beauty and the Beast, Little Shop of Horrors, Be Our Guest Restaurant\n- Organizations: Walt Disney Pictures\n- Topics: songs, musicals, animated films, film adaptations, naming references\n\nFacts:\n- Howard Elliott Ashman was an American playwright and lyricist who lived from May 17, 1950 to March 14, 1991.\n- Howard Ashman directed and wrote both the book and lyrics for the musical Little Shop of Horrors, which debuted in 1982.\n- Little Shop of Horrors became a long-running success and later led to a 1986 feature film.\n- Walt Disney Pictures released Beauty and the Beast as its 30th animated feature film in 1991.\n- Howard Ashman and Alan Menken wrote the song “Be Our Guest” for Walt Disney Pictures’ animated film Beauty and the Beast.\n- Be Our Guest Restaurant takes its name from “Be Our Guest,” a song from Beauty and the Beast.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
